<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94440" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίττᾰ</span></b> , a cry of drovers to urge on or guide
		their flocks (<i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>st!</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίττα, νέμεσθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					8.69
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίτθ᾽, ὁ λέπαργος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.45
				</span></i>
			; when <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό</span> follows, to drive
			them off, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀπὸ τᾶς κράνας σίττ᾽,
				ἀμνίδες</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίττ᾽ ἀπὸ τᾶς κοτίνω</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				100
			</span></i>; when <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός</span> follows, to lead
			them on, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίτθ᾽, ἁ Κυμαίθα, ποτὶ τὸν λόφον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.46
				</span></i>
			: cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψίττα, ψύττα</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
